From 343880a14098ae7e5e25e9320621e2d4df1e872a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 16:24:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0238 -- Campaign 3 GUS: MidiBackendGus + GM .pat loader
 + AUDIO_BACKEND=gus

Native Gravis Ultrasound (GF1) wavetable music on a no-Sound-Blaster card
(real GUS or PicoGUS /mode gus). Structurally the AdLib path: out-of-band
(no SDL audio device, no SDL3_mixer), clocked by the shared PIT/IRQ-0 pump
(SDL/0110), brought up via the SDL/0112 GF1 exports. GM instruments render
on the GF1's hardware voices from GUS .pat samples uploaded to card DRAM.

Why DOS needs this: a GUS-only box has no Sound Blaster, so SDL_INIT_AUDIO
cannot open an SB device and the SB IRQ-5 MIDI clock never fires. The gus
boot-mode omits SDL_INIT_AUDIO but keeps SoundManager::init (mirroring the
adlib FOURTH boot mode), brings the GF1 up out-of-band, and clocks MIDI off
the card-agnostic PIT pump. .pat file I/O + float pitch precompute happen at
on_song_start (main-loop); note_on/program_change run in the PIT IRQ and
touch only resident DRAM with integer-only math (no I/O/malloc/FPU in ISR).
Per-song lazy .pat residency bounded by the <=1MB GF1 DRAM. MUSIC ONLY this
phase (#27); GF1 SFX = #28.

The two SB-device-open gates (MIX_Init + MIX_CreateMixerDevice) are widened
to the gus path too (not just adlib) -- otherwise the gus path fell through
to opening a nonexistent SB device and fataled at boot (no-SB GUS-only box).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
